Two side observations from the live karr #101 capture run, 2026-08-24. Both verified against
real AKI.IO responses; neither is urgent, both are POD-worthy at minimum.

1) THINKING IS DROPPED ON THE OPENAI SHIM

Captured AKIOpenAI tool-call response carries the model reasoning under "reasoning":

  "message":{"role":"assistant",
             "reasoning":"The user wants me to add 7 and 15 using the add tool.",
             "tool_calls":[...]}

Role::OpenAICompatible::chat_response:371 reads only reasoning_content:

  defined $msg->{reasoning_content} ? ( thinking => $msg->{reasoning_content} ) : (),

so $response->thinking is undef although the model reasoning is on the wire. Compare the
Anthropic shim on the identical prompt, which DOES surface it (thinking block -> ->thinking
populated). Same provider, same model, reasoning visible on one route only.

reasoning_content is the DeepSeek/NousResearch spelling and is correct for them; the bare
"reasoning" spelling is what AKI ships. Whoever fixes this should check whether accepting
both in the shared role is right, or whether it belongs in an AKI-side override -- the role
is shared by ~25 engines, so widening it is not free. Do not widen on this single data point
without checking what the other providers actually send.

Fixture: akiopenai_tool_call_response.json

2) CLIENT ERRORS ARRIVE AS HTTP 529 / overloaded_error

Capture 5 with max_tokens=64 returned:

  <- 529 UNKNOWN
  {"type":"error","error":{"type":"overloaded_error",
    "message":"Response finished before tool_call was completed! Try to raise
               max_gen_tokens (or max_tokens in OpenAI or Anthropic Interface)"}}

The condition is a caller-side token budget too small to finish a tool_call -- deterministic,
reproducible, and fixed by raising max_tokens (the identical request at 512 returned 200 OK).
AKI reports it as 529 overloaded_error, i.e. as transient server overload.

Langertha carries no retry/backoff layer today (grepped: nothing in lib/), so nothing inside
the distribution misbehaves right now. The hazard is downstream: any consumer -- or any future
Langertha retry policy -- that treats 429/529 as "wait and retry" will loop forever on a
request that can never succeed at that token budget, and pay for every attempt.

Worth a POD warning on Engine::AKIAnthropic / Engine::AKIOpenAI, and worth remembering if a
retry layer is ever added: AKI 529 is not a reliable overload signal, the error.message text
is the real diagnostic.

Fixed in ca56b86. Part 1 (reasoning dropped): lifted AKI's bare 'reasoning' key onto Response.thinking via an AKI-scoped around chat_response (VLLMHook precedent), NOT by widening the shared OpenAICompatible role. Part 2 (529 overloaded_error): POD warnings on AKIOpenAI + AKIAnthropic that AKI returns deterministic caller-side errors as 529, with error.message as the diagnostic. New t/27_akiopenai_requests.t covers part 1.

Orchestrator review 2026-09-01: diff ca56b86 verified. AKI-scoped around chat_response, reasoning_content precedence kept, shared role untouched; 529 POD on both shims. Note for follow-up: the lift covers chat_response only - the streaming path drops thinking for the WHOLE OpenAI family (Stream::Chunk has no thinking field, parse_stream_chunk reads delta.content only), filed as its own ticket. Closing.
